.TH EXECUTE 1 "October 2026" "execute 0.9.0-rc.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
execute \- readable Unix workflows with declarative applets and direct pipes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B execute
.I FILE
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fIARG\fR...]
.br
.B execute
.B check|explain|inspect|run
.I FILE
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B execute resume
.I FILE
.B \-\-checkpoint
.I DIR
.br
.B execute
.BR test | run-parts | show-run | replay | repl | repair | compile | checkpoint | help | attach | dap | daemon
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ]
.br
.B execute applets
.BR list|inspect|discover|match
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B execute modules
.BR inspect|verify|lock
.I MANIFEST
.br
.B execute service generate
.BR systemd|launchd
.I FILE
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B execute lsp
.RB [ \-\-stdio ]
.br
.B execute live
.IR SUBCOMMAND ...
.br
.B execute model
.BR classify|judge|score|generate|extract
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Execute runs
.I .program
files: typed glue that starts native commands and manifest applets, moves their
output through direct pipes, and reports what it will do. Computation belongs to
applets, not to the language. Use
.B execute check
to validate a program without running anything, and
.B execute explain
to see the effects a program would have.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check \fIFILE\fR
Validate a program without running it. Add
.B \-\-json
for a structured result.
.TP
.B explain \fIFILE\fR
Show each step and its declared effects. Add
.B \-\-json
for a machine-readable plan, which includes the declared flags and options.
.TP
.B inspect \fIFILE\fR
Describe the program's inputs, including flags, options and their sources, without
running it.
.TP
.B run \fIFILE\fR
Run the program. Arguments after
.B \-\-
are passed to the program's declared inputs. Use
.B run \fIFILE\fR \fB\-\- \-\-help\fR
for the help generated from its declarations.
.TP
.B resume \fIFILE\fR \fB\-\-checkpoint\fR \fIDIR\fR
Continue a checkpointed run from its last durable step.
.TP
.B test
Run program tests using answers supplied by the test configuration or
.BR \-\-answers .
.TP
.B run-parts \fIDIR\fR
Run eligible programs in a directory.
.TP
.B show-run \fIDIR\fR
Display a recorded run.
.TP
.B replay \fIDIR\fR
Replay a recorded run without repeating refused effects.
.TP
.B repl
Start the interactive interpreter.
.TP
.B repair \fIFILE\fR
Inspect and repair a checkpointed program run.
.TP
.B compile
Compile a supported program form, including POSIX sh output.
.TP
.B checkpoint status \fIDIR\fR
Report checkpoint state; add \fB\-\-json\fR for structured output.
.TP
.B help
Show command help.
.TP
.B attach \fIPATH\fR
Connect to a live run control endpoint.
.TP
.B dap
Run the Debug Adapter Protocol server.
.TP
.B daemon
Serve, inspect or stop the per-user run daemon.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-input " NAME=VALUE"
Supply a declared program input. May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Structured result for
.B check
and
.BR explain .
.TP
.BI \-\-answers " FILE"
Answers file for
.BR test .
.TP
.BI \-\-record " DIR"
Record a finite run for inspection or replay.
.TP
.B \-\-what-if
Print the run plan and review fingerprint without running it.
.TP
.BI \-\-confirm " FINGERPRINT"
Run only when the current plan matches a reviewed fingerprint.
.TP
.BI \-\-allow " CAPABILITY"
Grant a capability for the effects gate. May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-policy-header
Include the capability policy header in explain output.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
Select output format: \fBgithub\fR or \fBjson\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-single-instance " FILE"
Prevent concurrent runs with an exclusive lock file.
.TP
.B \-\-control
Enable the live control socket for a run.
.TP
.BI \-\-break-at " LINE"
Pause execution at a source line for debugging.
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Forward a run through the per-user daemon when available.
.TP
.B \-\-json-errors
Emit structured runtime errors on standard error. Place before \fB\-\-\fR.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run a UI once and print JSON state.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Run one calendar activation and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-init
Supervise a worker as PID 1 (Unix).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-runs " N"
Maximum trigger runs or interactive UI jobs.
.TP
.BI \-\-missed\-ticks " POLICY"
Select trigger backlog handling policy.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-catch\-up " N"
Bound catch-up runs to 1 through 64.
.TP
.BI \-\-calendar\-dedup " MODE"
Select calendar fold deduplication mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-record\-bytes " N"
Maximum listener or stream record size in bytes.
.TP
.BI \-\-manifest\-dir " DIR"
Directory containing applet manifests. Defaults to the installed manifests.
.TP
.BI \-\-manifest\-catalog " FILE"
Packed manifest catalog. Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-manifest\-dir .
.TP
.BI \-\-capability\-policy " FILE"
Enforce a versioned applet policy for
.BR check ", " explain ", " inspect ", " run ", " resume ", " live .
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-flow\-policy " FILE"
Enforce origin and persistence data-flow grants.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-dir " DIR"
Cache directory for
.B run
and
.BR resume .
.TP
.BI \-\-checkpoint " DIR"
Durable checkpoint directory for
.B run
and
.BR resume .
.TP
.B \-\-retry\-uncertain
Retry an invocation whose prior outcome is uncertain. Only with
.BR resume .
.TP
.B \-\-trace
Print execution details to standard error.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-output\-bytes " N"
Largest captured output, in bytes.
.TP
.BI \-\-command\-timeout\-ms " N"
Lifetime limit for each native pipeline.
.TP
.BI \-\-total\-timeout\-ms " N"
Lifetime limit for the whole workflow.
.TP
.BI \-\-drain\-timeout\-ms " N"
Budget for an interrupt to finish running work before the run is cancelled. Default
10000. Only with
.BR run .
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the command help, or with a program file and
.B \-\-
the program's generated help.
.PP
Options that take values require a separate following argument; the
.B \-\-option=value
form is not accepted. The same usage text is printed by
.B \-\-help
and on argument errors.
.SH EXIT STATUS
A program's explicit
.B exit with status
value is its exit status. A failing native command reports its own status. An
interrupt exits with 130 after any drain.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/execute/manifests
Bundled applet manifests, found from the installed binary's location.
.TP
.I /usr/share/execute/docs
Language and platform documentation.
.TP
.I /usr/share/execute/editors
Editor grammar for syntax highlighting.
.SH SEE ALSO
The language reference in
.IR /usr/share/execute/docs .
